official [71f334935]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.stable.mono - Windows 10 (build 17134) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1070 (NVIDIA; 31.0.15.3141) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-7700 CPU @ 3.60GHz (8 threads) - 23.92 GiB memory - WASAPI (96000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe `Load as Placeholder` flag is not properly updated when running your game.\n\nGodot only updates the placeholder status when saving the scene manually (_Ctrl+S_). \nSo running the game _(with F5 or F6_) and having the scene auto-save executes the game with wrong placeholder status.\n\n**I seems the problem is that changing the `Load as Placeholder` options does not set the scene as dirty. \nSo Godot does not save it before running.\nThere is also no DoUndo action generated for changing the `Load as Placeholder`.**\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a71d3b6e-a872-4988-afe1-4b08c66df311\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a scene, and add an instanced scene inside it.\n- Save the scene manually first.\n- Set the instanced scene with Load as Placeholder.\n- Press Run or hotkey to Run Scene\n\n**Result:** Scene is loaded normally, not as Placeholder\n**Expected:** Scene not loaded (loaded as placeholder)\n\nThe same happens in reverse.\nPlaceholder status only updates when saving the scene manually.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[placeholder MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29549808/placeholder.MRP.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.c